  "result": "I added `plural(count, noun)` in `src/core/plural.ts` and committed it as 5b38c80. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Behavior:** `plural(1, 'file')` gives `1 file`, and `plural(2, 'file')` and `plural(0, 'file')` give `2 files` and `0 files`. It only appends an `s`, so irregular plurals are not handled.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/plural.test.ts` uses node:test and covers one, two and zero.\n- **Shard weight:** I gave the new test a weight of 0.1 in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`, as the repo requires.\n- **No helper reused:** `src/` had no existing pluralizing helper. The nearby code writes `=== 1 ? '' : 's'` inline, as in `src/ci/logs.ts` and `src/task/claims.ts`. Core also can't import from outside itself, so the function stands alone. I left those inline uses alone.\n- **Commit title has no task id:** The convention says to end it with the task id, but no id was in your brief. If you give me one, I can amend the commit.",
